// REJECTED — bitwise operators are Int32-only (item 366, docs/arithmetic.md).
// A bit pattern is a fixed-width object; Int (64-bit, arbitrary-precision on
// the python/TypeScript hosts) and Float have no uniform bitwise meaning across
// the six tiers, so the operators are restricted to Int32 rather than shipping a
// per-tier divergence. Narrow an Int with `.to_int32()` to take its bits.
//
// expected error:
//   `|` requires `Int32` operands, got `Float`

fn flags(a: Float, b: Float) -> Int32 {
  return a | b
}
